�Prigodi malen'kogo sirogo Misheniatka til'ki pochinaiut'sia!
Iz malen'koyi zatishnoyi nirki vono potrapliaie u velikii, prostorii, spovnenii div i riznobarv'ia svit. U nastupnikh knizhkakh seriyi iomu dovedet'sia shche bagato pomandruvati, vidshukati chimalo tsikavinok, spiznati vsiliakikh radoshchiv i prigod. Zaraz u serden'ku golovnogo geroia zhevriie mriia pobachiti iakomoga bil'she kol'oriv - ale poki pered nim lezhit' lishe neosiazhne zasnizhene pole... Kudi zh privede Misheniatka iogo persha mandrivka?"�
�For some people falling in love was a happy, glowing experience. For Briar Kelly and Arrow Donovan it was more like getting hit by a freight train.
Caring for one another was never an easy feat. They constantly fought to hold their feelings inside, not wanting to jeopardize their friendship. Then, Arrow left for the Marines, and everything changed. Briar was shattered. Arrow was hurt.
While Briar told herself she'd never let another man affect her in such a way, Arrow still remained in the forefront of her mind. For Arrow, his memories of Briar kept him alive in both of his near death experiences. When Arrow's demons threatened to drag him under, Briar was there, pulling him from the darkness.
"What ifs" keep piling up while resentment and redemption battles continue; will Briar and Arrow be able to find their happily ever after, or will this be one war that Arrow can't win?
This is a standalone, contemporary romance. Due to language and sexual content, this book is not intended for readers under the age of 18."�
�The bestselling author of Blaze presents a heart-pounding account of the world's greatest nuclear disaster, based on sources not available before the fall of the Soviet Union. Read's enthralling account is filled with acts of courage--and also bumbling confusion, secrecy, lies, and coverups. Read spent many months in Russia interviewing hundreds of survivors and experts. Photographs. 3 maps."�
�Музичні інструменти українського народу (Серія "Слобожанський світ". Випуск 4)"�
�Druga redaktsiia knigi "Muzichni instrumenti ukrayins'kogo narodu" korifeia ukrayins'koyi kul'turi Gnata Martinovicha Khotkevicha (1877-1938) chekala na svoiu publikatsiiu 75 rokiv.
Porivniano z pershoiu redaktsiieiu (Kharkiv, 1930), druga redaktsiia bezsmertnoyi i iedinoyi u svoiemu rodi pratsi Gnata Khotkevicha ne lishe vdvichi bil'sha za obsiagom, a i maie vidminnosti na kontseptual'nomu i teoretichnomu rivniakh.
Kniga proiliustrovana raritetnimi zobrazhenniami, dopovnena tsikavimi fotobiografichnimi materialami ta fakhovimi stattiami naikrashchikh instrumentoznavtsiv suchasnosti.
Vidannia priurocheno do 135-richchiu vid dnia narodzhennia avtora."�
�Didusi isnuiut', shchob loviti z onukami ribu i vchiti yikh svistati - tak gadaie Ul'f i perekonuie v ts'omu svogo druga Berru. I ne bida, shcho v Berri didusia nemaie - ie mistse, de iogo mozhna znaiti. Tak geroyi povisti <>znaiomliat'sia z didusem Nil'som, i tsia druzhba daie yim naivazhlivishii u zhitti dosvid chuinosti ta liubovi.
Ul'f maie naikrashchu u sviti sestru, iaka ne vereshchit' i ne smikaie iogo za chuba. Adzhe vona - angel. Takoiu yiyi uiavliaie sobi Ul'f, tomu z nim vidbuvaiut'sia kumedni prigodi.
1996 roku knizhka <>z iliustratsiiami vidomoyi shveds'koyi khudozhnitsi Anni Geg'lund otrimala naiprestizhnishu u Shvetsiyi vidznaku Augustpriset (premiiu im. Avg'usta Strindberg'a) u nominatsiyi <>.
Knizhku vidano za pidtrimki Shveds'koyi radi z pitan' kul'turi KULTURRADET."�
�Hayato Tachibana is a 27 year-old assistant at Cosmos University who pursues his research on global warming in his spare time.
One night, upon getting stumped while writing his thesis, he notices the stack of Real Maid boxes that have been sitting dormant in his room for over half a year. On a whim, he examines the parts contained in one of the boxes, and decides to put them together.
Several clicks and whirrs later, a Real Maid stands completed before his eyes...
So begins the tale of the peculiar and fantasy-filled life of Hayato and Moe!"�
�The first in a series of adventures of 18-year-old Lexi. In this story, we meet Lexi for the first time. Blonde, beautiful and hard to resist. She has her eye on her older, married neighbor, and nothing is going to stop her from getting her man. A story of forbidden lust, with a rather unexpected twist."�
�Avtobiograficheskaia povest' Viktora Iuzefovicha Dragunskogo "On upal na travu" otkryvaet novuiu, "voennuiu" seriiu "Samokata". Nazvanie serii - "Kak eto bylo" - ob'iasniaet izdatel'skii zamysel: rasskazat' o Velikoi Otechestvennoi voine 1941-1945 godov chestno i ob'ektivno - nastol'ko, naskol'ko eto vozmozhno. Chestnost' garantiruiut imena avtorov - eto russkie pisateli-frontoviki, neposredstvennye ochevidtsy opisyvaemogo, liudi s bezuprechnoi lichnoi i tvorcheskoi reputatsiei. Ob'ektivnost', my nadeemsia, obespechit "nauchnyi apparat": v kazhdoi knige serii khudozhestvennoe proizvedenie dopolniaetsia stat'ioi istorika, izlagaiushchei segodniashnii vzgliad na opisyvaemye sobytiia. Pervaia kniga serii "Kak eto bylo" rasskazyvaet o sud'be moskovskogo opolcheniia, o tragedii oseni 1941 goda: ne prizvannye v deistvuiushchuiu armiiu (po zdorov'iu, vozrastu i t.p.) moskvichi dobrovol'tsami otpravliaiutsia na ryt'io okopov i stalkivaiutsia - neobuchennye, neobmundirovannye i dazhe ne vooruzhennye, - s nikem uzhe v tot moment ne sderzhivaemoi volnoi nemetskogo nastupleniia."�
�U Peg'fordi na sorok p'iatomu rotsi zhittia raptovo pomiraie chlen mistsevoyi radi Barri Ferbrazer. Tsia podiia shokuvala mistian.
U provintsiinomu angliis'komu zatishnomu mistechku z brukovanim maidanom i starodavnim monastirem, zdavalosia b, panuie idiliia, ale vseredini mistechka, za tsim privablivim fasadom, tochit'sia spravzhnia viina. Zamozhni voiuiut' z ubogimi, pidlitki -- z bat'kami, zhinki -- zi svoyimi cholovikami, vchiteli -- z uchniami...
Nespodivana vakansiia u peg'fords'kii radi nevdovzi maie vsi shansi sprovokuvati mistechko na chi ne naibil'shu v iogo istoriyi viinu. Khto stane peremozhtsem na viborakh, de panuiut' pristrasti, dvorushnist' i nespodivani vikrittia?
Tse velikii roman pro malen'ke mistechko i persha knizhka Dzhoan Roling' dlia doroslikh. Zakhoplivii tvir, stvorenii nezrivniannim opovidachem."�

�
U travni 2013 roku, za krok vid omriianoyi medichnoyi ta naukovoyi kar'ieri, Pol Kalaniti diagnostuvav u sebe rak legeniv 4-yi stadiyi i rozpochav svoiu knigu. Krapku v nii postavila iogo smert' navesni 2015-go. A za desiat' misiatsiv vidverta ta muzhnia istoriia borot'bi, kokhannia i samoviddanoyi likars'koyi pratsi stala bestselerom No. 1 za versiieiu The New York Times ta uviishla do lideriv prodazhiv na Amazon.com.
Vrazhaiucha spovid' talanovitogo neirokhirurga, iakii zakhvoriv u 35 rokiv. <>Pomirati vid raku v molodomu vitsi i znati, shcho tvii vipadok -- odin na desiat' tisiach. Bezlich raziv povidomliati khvorim pro strashnii diagnoz, virishuvati, chiie zhittia mozhlivo vriatuvati, a chiie ni, -- i raptom samomu opinitisia na likarnianomu lizhku i chekati viroku, skil'ki tobi zalishilosia. Nazavzhdi rozproshchatisia z mriiami pro skladni operatsiyi ta naukovu pratsiu... A todi zrozumiti: inshogo vzhe ne bude i pravil'ne zapitannia <>. I, zabuvshi pro bil', priiti do operatsiinoyi, zhiti, kokhati -- i vziati na ruki novonarodzhenu donechku...
Tsia zvorushliva ta nadikhaiucha istoriia tak i zalishit'sia nedopisanoiu. Bo tse -- istoriia pro zhittia, a ne pro smert', istoriia, shcho vchit' muzhnosti, stiikosti, virnosti profesiinomu obov'iazku ta vminniu pobachiti v strashnomu diagnozi ne virok, a shans zrobiti zhittia nemarnim."�
�Tse kniga-viklik, kniga-provokatsiia. Tse rozpovid' pro te, shcho ne afishuiut', shcho obgovoriuiut' u duzhe tisnomu tovaristvi -- i shcho stanovit' bil'shu chastinu us'ogo internet-trafiku. Pro porno. Pro glasni i neglasni pravila ts'ogo <>kino, z iogo zirkovimi rezhiserami, khalturnim treshem, vlasnim <>i mifami pro manlivu dostupnist'. Pro zruinovani stereotipi i prigolomshlivi odkrovennia. Tse istoriia divchini z ukrayins'koyi provintsiyi, iaka znaishla adrenalin, osobistu svobodu i uliublenu robotu na znimal'nomu maidanchiku za shchil'no zapnutimi viknami. Utim, poshuki sebe trivaiut'."�
�Kniga pro 242 dni boyiv v aeroportu Donets'ka, abo v ADu -- iak iogo nazvali oborontsi letovishcha -- tse maizhe shist' desiatkiv svidchen' <>, komentari viis'kovikh ekspertiv ta viis'kovikh analitikiv z Ukrayini, Rosiyi, SShA ta Kanadi, predstavnika General'nogo shtabu Zbroinikh sil Ukrayini. Ale golovne -- pro zhittia i smert', pro vidchaidushnist' i strakh, pro liubov i druzhbu, pro te -- shcho i chomu zakhishchali u terminalakh DAPu ukrayins'ki biitsi -- chitaite u rozpovidiakh bezposerednikh uchasnikiv oboroni Donets'kogo aeroportu. Chitaite, analizuite ta robit' svoyi neuperedzheni visnovki!"�
�When the King's governor, after falling into rebel hands and changing sides, is recaptured by royal troops and executed, his sons and grandsons are also condemned to death. They survive by subterfuge, but they have lost their place in society. The Poettells the story of Kim, the youngest grandson, consigned to a life of vagrancy and genteel begging as a wandering poet. In his efforts to recover the family's fortunes, he commits a second betrayal, this time against his own house. This is a haunting and luminous tale whose main themes are the search for self-respect and self-identity in an unjust society."�
�Mnogie vzroslye mechtatel'no vspominaiut "prekrasnyi i bezzabotnyi vozrast", no v glubine dushi sodrogaiutsia ot uzhasa i raduiutsia, chto "vsio proshlo". Strashno, kogda tvoio telo meniaetsia i perestaiot slushat'sia, strashno stat' predmetom nasmeshek sverstnikov. Strashno byt' ne takim, kak vse. No eshchio strashnee - okazat'sia vmeste s bol'shinstvom."�
�Marshall Boswell examines the four major works of fiction David Foster Wallace has produced thus far: the novels The Broom of the System and Infinite Jest and the story collections Girl with Curious Hair and Brief Interviews with Hideous Men."�
�Do knigi vviishli 45 eseyiv, iaki vpershe pobachili svit u 2012-2013 rokakh na shpal'takh gazeti <>v rubritsi <>. U nikh avtor porushuie tsilu nizku pitan', vazhlivikh dlia kozhnoyi liudini: shchastia, svoboda, liubov, pravda, poeziia, samotnist'... A geroiami eseyiv ie i dobre vidomi vsim klasiki, zokrema Skovoroda, Kvitka-Osnov'ianenko, Shevchenko, Gogol', Dragomanov, Franko, Lesia Ukrayinka, Kobilians'ka, Vinnichenko, Khvil'ovii, Iogansen, Malaniuk, Dovzhenko, Ianovs'kii, i kudi menshe znani avtori: Krims'kii, Shpol, Burevii, Chernov, Teliga, Livits'ka-Kholodna i inshi. Napisani v iaskravii publitsistichnii maneri, tsi <>nezaperechno svidchat' pro odne: ukrayins'ka literaturna traditsiia vid davnini do s'ogodni - bagata, barvista i nadzvichaino tsikava."�
�Do knizhki uviishli vibrani tvori Mikoli Khvil'ovogo (1893-- 1933) -- ukrayins'kogo prozayika, poeta, publitsista, odnogo z osnovopolozhnikiv porevoliutsiinoyi ukrayins'koyi prozi. Noveli prozayika i s'ogodni privabliuiut' chitacha ne lishe tematichnoiu zlobodennistiu, a i stil'ovoiu, mistets'koiu samobutnistiu. Dobir podanikh tekstiv obumovlenii shkil'noiu programoiu z ukrayins'koyi literaturi. Rozrakhovana na shkoliariv, vchiteliv, studentiv-filologiv, usikh, khto tsikavit'sia tvorchistiu M. Khvil'ovogo."	
